ed"}],"gloss":"having conquered","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"அகத்து","parts":[{"text":"அகத்து","lemma":"அகத்து","gloss":"inside"}],"gloss":"inside","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"அடக்கிய","parts":[{"text":"அடக்கு","lemma":"அடக்கு","gloss":"contain"},{"text":"இய","lemma":"இய","gloss":"relative participle"}],"gloss":"contained"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தண்டா","parts":[{"text":"தண்டா","lemma":"தண்டு","gloss":"unceasing"}],"gloss":"unceasing"},{"surface":"ஈகைத்","parts":[{"text":"ஈகை","lemma":"ஈகை","gloss":"generosity"},{"text":"த்","lemma":"த்","gloss":"sandhi"}],"gloss":"generosity"},{"surface":"தகைமாண்","parts":[{"text":"தகை","lemma":"தகை","gloss":"quality"},{"text":"மாண்","lemma":"மாண்","gloss":"glorious"}],"gloss":"glorious in quality"},{"surface":"குடுமி","parts":[{"text":"குடுமி","lemma":"குடுமி","gloss":"Kuṭumi"}],"gloss":"Kuṭumi"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தண்கதிர்","parts":[{"text":"தண்","lemma":"தண்","gloss":"cool"},{"text":"கதிர்","lemma":"கதிர்","gloss":"rays"}],"gloss":"cool-rayed"},{"surface":"மதியம்","parts":[{"text":"மதியம்","lemma":"மதியம்","gloss":"moon"}],"gloss":"moon"},{"surface":"போலவும்","parts":[{"text":"போல","lemma":"போல","gloss":"like"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"and"}],"gloss":"and like"},{"surface":"தெறுசுடர்","parts":[{"text":"தெறு","lemma":"தெறு","gloss":"scorch"},{"text":"சுடர்","lemma":"சுடர்","gloss":"glow"}],"gloss":"scorching-rayed"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஒண்கதிர்","parts":[{"text":"ஒண்கதிர்","lemma":"ஒண்கதிர்","gloss":"bright-rayed"}],"gloss":"bright-rayed","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"ஞாயிறு","parts":[{"text":"ஞாயிறு","lemma":"ஞாயிறு","gloss":"sun"}],"gloss":"sun"},{"surface":"போலவும்","parts":[{"text":"போல","lemma":"போல","gloss":"like"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"and"}],"gloss":"and like"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மன்னிய","parts":[{"text":"மன்னு","lemma":"மன்னு","gloss":"endure"},{"text":"இய","lemma":"இய","gloss":"optative"}],"gloss":"may you endure"},{"surface":"பெரும","parts":[{"text":"பெரும","lemma":"பெருமான்","gloss":"O great one"}],"gloss":"O great one"},{"surface":"நீ","parts":[{"text":"நீ","lemma":"நீ","gloss":"you"}],"gloss":"you"},{"surface":"நிலமிசையானே","parts":[{"text":"நிலம்","lemma":"நிலம்","gloss":"earth"},{"text":"மிசை","lemma":"மிசை","gloss":"upon"},{"text":"ஆனே","lemma":"ஆனே","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"upon the earth"}]}],"literal":"To the north of the unfading, snow-capped tall mountain / To the south of the fear-inspiring Kumari / To the east of the shore-battering dug-out sea / To the west of the ancient, old ocean / Below, even below the depth of the water-world of the three-fold joined ordered first structure / Above, even in the world of cows, unceasingly / Having become form and fame, like the examining pointer of a balance scale, without bias / May your side excel! / In the land of the enemies who opposed your actions of war / Your ocean-like army submerging, surging, commanding properly the dense, spotted, small-eyed elephants / Capturing many difficult fortresses with green-pastured gardens / Bestowing the fine ornaments obtained from those fortresses to the needy people according to their merit / May your umbrella bow down only to circumambulate the temple of the three-eyed Lord! / May your head bow down, O great one, before the raised hands of the sages of the four Vedas! / May your garland wither, O Lord, only because of the blowing of the fragrant smoke from burning the enemies' lands! / May your anger go away only before the bright faces of your sulking, bright-jewelled women! / Thus, having conquered all victories and contained them within / O Kuṭumi of glorious quality and unceasing generosity! / Like the cool-rayed moon and like the scorching-rayed, bright sun / May you endure upon this earth, O great one!","translation":"To the north of the unfading, snow-capped Himalayas, to the south of the awe-inspiring Kumari, to the east of the shore-battering ocean, and to the west of the ancient sea; below the depths of the underworld, and above the heavens, your form and fame spread unceasingly. Like the needle of a balanced scale, you rule without bias; may your reign excel! You sent your ocean-like army to submerge the lands of the enemies who opposed you, commanding your spotted, small-eyed elephants to capture their fortresses. The fine ornaments taken from those forts, you bestowed upon the needy according to their merit. May your royal umbrella bow only when circumambulating the temple of the three-eyed Lord Shiva! May your head bow, O great king, only before the raised hands of the sages of the four Vedas! May your garland wither only from the fragrant smoke of burning enemy lands! May your anger vanish only before the bright faces of your sulking, beautifully jewelled wives! O Kuṭumi of glorious quality and unceasing generosity, who has gathered all victories within yourself! Like the cool-rayed moon and the fierce, bright sun, may you endure forever upon this earth!","modern":"வாடாத பனிபொருந்திய இமயமலைக்கு வடக்கிலும், அச்சம் தரும் குமரிமுனைக்குத் தெற்கிலும், கரையை மோதும் தோண்டப்பட்ட கடலுக்கு கிழக்கிலும், பழமையான கடலுக்கு மேற்கிலும், கீழே பாதாள உலகத்திற்கு அப்பாலும், மேலே தேவலோகத்திற்கு அப்பாலும் உனது புகழும் உருவமும் நிலைபெற்றுள்ளன. நடுநிலைமை தவறாத தராசின் முள் போல ஒரு பக்கமும் சாயாமல் உனது செங்கோல் சிறப்பதாக! போரிட்ட பகைவர்களின் நாடுகளில் உனது கடற்படை மூழ்கிப் பாய, புள்ளிகளையுடைய சிறிய கண்களைக் கொண்ட யானைகளைச் செலுத்தி, அவர்களின் மதில்களைக் கைப்பற்றினாய். அங்கிருந்து பெற்ற அணிகலன்களைப் பரிசில் பெறுவோருக்குத் தகுதிக்கேற்ப வழங்கினாய். உனது வெண்கொற்றக்குடை முக்கண் உடைய சிவபெருமானின் கோயிலை வலம் வரும்போது மட்டுமே பணியட்டும்! உனது தலை நான்கு மறைகளை ஓதும் அந்தணர்களின் கைகளுக்கு முன்னால் மட்டுமே பணியட்டும்! உனது மாலை பகைவர்களின் நாடுகளைச் சுட்டெரிக்கும் புகையினால் மட்டுமே வாடட்டும்! உனது சினம் சிறந்த அணிகலன்களை அணிந்த உனது மனைவியரின் ஊடல் முகத்திற்கு முன்னால் மட்டுமே தணியட்டும்! இவ்வாறு எல்லா வெற்றிகளையும் பெற்றுத் தன்னுள் அடக்கிய, கொடைத்திறம் மிக்க குடுமிப் பெருவழுதியே! குளிர்ந்த திங்களைப் போலவும், சுட்டெரிக்கும் ஞாயிறைப் போலவும் நீ இந்நிலவுலகில் பல்லாண்டு வாழ்வாயாக!","explanation":"This poem is addressed to the Pandyan king Palyāgasālai Mudukuṭumi Peruvaḻuti by the poet Kārikiḻār under the Pāṭāṇ tiṇai. The poet praises the king's vast domain, which extends beyond the traditional boundaries of the Tamil land, and compares his absolute justice to a perfectly balanced scale. He wishes that the king's royal umbrella should bow only to circumambulate the temple of Lord Shiva, and his head should bow only to the raised hands of Vedic sages. His anger should cool down only before his sulking wives, and his garland should wither only from the smoke of burning enemy territories. Finally, the poet blesses the king to live forever, combining the coolness of the moon and the fierce brilliance of the sun.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}